THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

This project implements the algorithm described in:

    Niv Cohen and Yedid Hoshen,
    "Sub-Image Anomaly Detection with Deep Pyramid Correspondences",
    arXiv:2005.02357, 2020.

Configuration and hyper-parameters are aligned with the third-party PyTorch
implementation `byungjae89/SPADE-pytorch` (MIT License) so that the reported
numbers can be checked against a public baseline. That repository is NOT an
official release by the paper's authors; no public repository from the paper's
authors was found.

Not to be confused with `NVlabs/SPADE`, an unrelated image-synthesis method
(spatially-adaptive normalization) that shares the acronym.

The MVTec Anomaly Detection dataset is NOT distributed with this repository.
It is released by MVTec Software GmbH under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for non-commercial
research use only: https://www.mvtec.com/company/research/datasets/mvtec-ad

Pretrained Wide-ResNet50-2 ImageNet weights are obtained from torchvision
(BSD-3-Clause).
